2026-10-23: Darwin SDK header sweep for the D19 exit.

Compiler: the debug evocc of ed7e423f, --target=aarch64-apple-darwin, at -O0
and at -O2, -S -o /dev/null. Reference: Apple clang 21.0.0 (clang-2100.1.1.101)
with -std=gnu17 -fsyntax-only, macOS SDK 26.5. Units: 1,900 files, each one
#include of an SDK or framework header (the units of the October 21 sweep).

Counts:
  units                                   1,900
  candidates (Apple clang compiles alone) 1,496
  EvoCC compiles at -O0 and at -O2        1,443
  EvoCC refuses at both levels               53
  refusals that a D19 rule keeps             53
  open refusals                               0

Kept refusals, by the rule that keeps them:
  Blocks, 21 units:
    19 report E2963 at a Blocks declarator (AppleEXR.h, SecTransform.h,
       MDItem.h, ESClient.h, odmoduleconfig.h).
     1 notify.h:336 reports E1004 at `bool`: notify.h includes
       <dispatch/dispatch.h>, which brings <stdbool.h>, only under __BLOCKS__.
       Apple clang with -fno-blocks fails at the same line.
     1 os/activity.h:161 reports E1001: os_block_t exists only with Blocks.
       Apple clang with -fno-blocks fails at the same line.
  overloadable, 2 units: E2964 (AppleArchive/AAHeader.h, tgmath.h).
  Clang vector types, 29 units: Spatial/Structures.h and StructuresFloat.h
    report E1004 at __API_AVAILABLE. <simd/base.h> declares nothing unless
    __has_attribute(__ext_vector_type__) and __has_attribute(__overloadable__)
    are true; EvoCC refuses both (E2967, E2964), so <simd/simd.h> also leaves
    __API_AVAILABLE undefined.
  GCC 14 refuses the construct, 1 unit: infiniband/verbs.h:1358 reports E2202.
    `struct ibv_modify_cq_attr` first appears inside a parameter list, so the
    call passes a pointer to another struct type. GCC 14 refuses the reduced
    construct (-Wincompatible-pointer-types is an error); Apple clang warns.

Evidence: .evidence/darwin-sdk-sweep-20261023/ (results.tsv, groups.md,
report.md, commands.log, candidates.txt, reference/).
